<title>KENYA: RALLYING-SAFARI RALLY RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>RALLYING-SAFARI RALLY RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI, Kenya 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results of the</p>
<p>Safari Rally ending on Monday:</p>
<p> 1. Colin McRae (Britain) Subaru    11 hours 29 minutes</p>
<p> 2. Richard Burns (Britain) Mitsubishi    11:36:04</p>
<p> 3. Ian Duncan (Kenya) Toyota		 11:40:18</p>
<p> 4. Armin Schwarz (Germany) Ford	    13:07:23</p>
<p> 5. Jonathan Toroitich (Kenya) Toyota)    13:49:32</p>
<p>Leading world championship standings (after three rounds):</p>
<p>1. McRae (Britain) Subaru 13 points</p>
<p>2. Carlos Sainz (Spain) Ford 12 points</p>
<p>3. Piero Liatti (Italy) Subaru 10 points</p>
<p>4. Kenneth Eriksson (Sweden) Subaru 10 points</p>
<p>5. Tommi Makinen (Finland) Mitsubishi 8 points</p>
<p>Manufacturers' championship:</p>
<p> 1. Subaru	33 points</p>
<p> 2. Ford	  19</p>
<p> 3. Mitsubishi  16</p>
